commit 317d4037cc983b85a7ca009bcb0316e51185e825
Author: ulala-x <ulalax@kairoscode.dev>
Date:   Thu Nov 5 19:06:10 2026 +0900

    perf(cpp): cut request submit heap allocations (#3867)
    
    Share request callable ownership, combine observer storage, borrow routing
    and serializer media data, reuse node wire-vector capacity, and reserve the
    complete node request header once. Keep public and physical replies separate
    with the same completion identity, ordering, and capture lifetime boundaries.
    
    The source submitter measures 49.466 -> 29.262 heap calls/message against
    the requested reference. Audited decision locations decrease 10 -> 9 by
    sharing the existing byte comparator; eight contract locations stay unchanged.
    Allocation references use borrowed inputs while retaining exact assertions.
    
    Spec: framework/doc/framework/common/spec/server/01-execution/01-submit-and-completion.ko.md:38
    Spec: framework/doc/framework/common/spec/server/01-execution/01-submit-and-completion.ko.md:329
    Spec: framework/doc/framework/common/spec/server/01-execution/01-submit-and-completion.ko.md:375
    Spec: framework/doc/framework/common/spec/server/01-execution/01-submit-and-completion.ko.md:490
    
    Validation: all affected C++ targets compiled with --parallel 3 and -k 0;
    296 unit/contract CTest entries and the Debug send allocation target passed;
    C++ format and diff checks passed. Allocation census and four-round
    Framework throughput comparisons are recorded in the job report.

